(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ab883447-23f3-4e64-b2a5-f9bbcfa44286"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"e7d14474-fdb8-4ea8-ae84-735c96a84c95"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"b96f265d-54d8-4bc8-92f2-c227b98ec88d"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"46359354-34f6-4b24-9a8c-e92beed7a706"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5752968c-7db3-4726-94c3-6cdf4b142d27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8c41e86b-4981-4aec-a4c8-e72db20d493b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"74b49499-e2bd-4c78-aceb-1be46c4fb3fa"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d653154a-6615-4963-8d01-544196f04b56"],

Cell["\<\
The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette also \
sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output matches the \
screen.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5776b484-85f8-4078-b996-68aa1a887195"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8bd87ab0-ed6a-447d-899b-7b15266da3ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ff7a2d18-8107-456c-b94f-e3f8ec5feea3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e6bdc773-3645-4de1-afe3-e677e8bfee3d"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"62dc945f-9c91-408d-a18e-666bdddf6101"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8da020a6-dea4-4b6d-8833-3a172360d23b"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cf33a61d-4c7c-4e0d-ab0b-2c8c033a56ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9a07cd4d-3269-45b3-9ac7-8852dae595eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tag cell",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " names a cell, and ",
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inserts a red bracketed link to that name \[LongDash] the two together \
give a bibliography: style each entry ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tag it, cite it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ffcbac06-cfd9-4194-9a94-d17bab7b2e45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"98dbff94-eaa4-4380-9c69-59f129519ed6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d2fe73d0-8988-448d-b58a-8cb6dc7b3524"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a bibliography tagged before that was true \[LongDash] or tagged \
through the Cell Tags dialog rather than the palette \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " labels every entry of a notebook at once, and clears the label of an entry \
whose tag you removed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8667a892-32fd-4155-ac4a-ff34de0441b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Existing tags are listed under ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ac6b8a72-2573-41e1-9d03-d1c6d277bfff"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8426396c-bf03-4350-bff1-e5a99a40903c"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"03e52601-c51d-41db-903e-dfbf0bff0701"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"77924b83-f1af-\
49e7-b66e-ba0d98383a08"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d68e634d-87a1-486b-b86a-eba2d81bd7a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3dc3d74a-4e16-48f5-9845-a4ea834c57b5"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f71a6f4a-967f-46e0-9110-19ed4c580c0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a fifth sheet and not a template: it is the notebook's own typography \
with the paper structure added, and it is what an imported paper opens on \
when its \\documentclass names no journal above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b2c23082-d8d2-4e1c-9a47-197a8c67d908"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d401854c-0dda-4e5e-bd2e-85e8b5819f0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"400b1899-93fe-498d-9869-9c56b2b8c11e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"01977cab-ee9a-448e-8a6a-0c48ff897171"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"669dc517-f098-4452-9ddf-2d8c994f6bac"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2cdf2146-8389-46a5-91d9-7f8e110aaf14"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7e63ba8c-c6f5-4f6e-9ac0-35ec932a732d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the rest of the prose with it \[LongDash] the title, the \
headings, the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography \
entries, and both kinds of list \[LongDash] so the document keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a864b5d6-047a-48bf-a430-b93eab80b8ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"85a9897b-79b3-47da-b3c5-40ef605b7051"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"65101410-bf0a-4909-9cbc-67342dab04a6"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c5beef12-f544-4297-8d1c-ef9406070523"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"af2b611d-4c81-4d02-a4af-6c77b45f20de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"857e1da7-57b9-4d66-b86b-bb3967868c09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"56bad00f-dc39-4b82-a0a8-f32e8cde2c34"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3e694825-6032-4947-a113-6b5b0b048423"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0a13d392-45df-4217-af52-0f06d2e9abd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"67ad3257-120e-4265-911c-0a11f37c34ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"52b2b898-cd1b-4016-b956-09191217345f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c215a9b5-fbff-4dac-a43e-795f300d6e9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"97ed156f-b8de-495d-9044-3ef5006dffa7"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e3203ae6-4723-427f-8ce7-9b2c561b9092"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d301fb92-ad49-4822-a2a7-bd19f89c804c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fa8a0a59-a9b3-4fd2-ae4f-92a75c9e431a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d68d48ab-a0af-4b4b-963e-0c645ef62c2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"43de550d-b0af-4cc0-a52d-bbb571d1467d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f4e08214-e004-486b-a296-87177110e51c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a29fc096-a4db-4723-acde-f9ec38401704"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"18f274b6-622a-40c8-83fb-e74ee243a137"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"044e882c-fc97-43bf-9365-3fb5ed0b06ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select the cells to convert, then press ",
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". With nothing selected the whole notebook is converted."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d2da5897-c35d-438d-add0-7c86e867d617"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b771edb9-c1e7-4a75-954c-c719c3ce6eca"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a13a9a7-cf64-41a3-9377-305125a3ea41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"47d55548-b1e2-4517-85b4-e38c9704bc93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1b1b4c64-8ec7-4c8d-aa64-a51f0c237440"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe. To bring in a LaTeX paper, paste it as Text cells and \
convert."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8d905901-3dd8-462e-8cee-a1dbe3dc326a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ImportLaTeXDocument[\"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads a whole paper instead: ",
 StyleBox["\\section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the theorem-like environments the preamble declares become cells of \
the matching style, ",
 StyleBox["\\label",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes a cell tag, ",
 StyleBox["\\ref",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\cite",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become live links, and ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXDocument",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes it back out. Anything it does not convert is carried verbatim, so \
what it cannot read it also does not damage."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1e5cdeba-25c6-4739-a8b0-679a69d5594a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The front matter comes with it: ",
 StyleBox["\\title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\date",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Title, Author and Date cells you can edit \[LongDash] the edit \
reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] and an ",
 StyleBox["abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes Abstract cells, headed once however many paragraphs it runs to. ",
 StyleBox["\\maketitle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has no content of its own, so it stays as text beside ",
 StyleBox["\\sloppy",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\tableofcontents",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1fe2a31a-49e1-4d8e-97b5-01d99cdb8e40"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["itemize",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["enumerate",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["description",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Item and ItemNumbered cells, one per ",
 StyleBox["\\item",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", nesting into Subitem and Subsubitem. Each list restarts its numbering as \
LaTeX does, an ",
 StyleBox["\\item[label]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " prints the label instead of the number, and a second paragraph of one item \
becomes an ItemParagraph cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bf786cf4-ac28-4184-ae0e-88df61ec6f0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["figure",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes its caption plus an ",
 StyleBox["Input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell holding the code that draws the picture \[LongDash] an ",
 StyleBox["Import",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the file the paper shipped, which you replace with the Wolfram code \
that generates it. Evaluate the cell and the figure is live; the picture's \
own markup, TikZ included, still goes back into the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " untouched, so the generating code stays the notebook's alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dbf9a5e9-5d03-43f7-91d8-9f5789480206"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bibliography comes in whichever way the paper writes it. A ",
 StyleBox["thebibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes one Reference cell per ",
 StyleBox["\\bibitem",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", each showing its key in brackets exactly as the citations to it read, and \
each is yours to edit \[LongDash] the edit reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Entries pulled from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become the same cells, but there the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " stays the source of truth: only the ",
 StyleBox["\\bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands go back out, so edit the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and re-import. A declared ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is not beside the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is reported rather than passed over in silence."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"00e5f17b-ac55-44cb-919c-412163312688"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"00662438-14f3-4b7b-b182-cf01e52d30c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the MaTeX buttons; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do \
not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"73a0feec-5de9-4695-b357-c03283b5a3ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3390a92b-ad7c-41af-a564-a2aa0b0fa68d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bcfc3d82-d5b8-4210-9253-c62d63c33b5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " renders the selected display equations through LaTeX; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " restores editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"97d05efa-3bb4-4273-9a32-982363acc315"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1e8f59c2-3cdc-401d-a9f0-ca43862bfd00"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f47fa945-a35b-4f7a-9734-7566721cb2bf"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"047f87a0-bf4a-491f-8a95-b6bb8432e05b"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"85342a4f-3dc9-49fc-89f6-5b12a51dc533"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4a230f93-fd28-4704-9bc3-d76ca156f1f1"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f0cf31d-f156-428a-afa4-a142b80b5771"],

Cell["\<\
Convert to LaTeX at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the \
notebook is the source.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"59610656-9842-4055-9880-a4801409b4e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and convert MaTeX cells back to math so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f573024-da68-494c-877b-dbeb39a81996"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"de5104a4-2ef6-4f1a-90ea-b0d505b4e113"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f72f91b0-04ff-4ed2-b1e3-315e43b85cf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nik Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[murzin]"]],
 CellTags->"murzin",ExpressionUUID->"a5d20090-0cd2-4bd9-a859-2c7672bdf221"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Szabolcs Horvat, MaTeX: LaTeX labels in Mathematica, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[matex]"]],
 CellTags->"matex",ExpressionUUID->"a332e110-9f8f-4c6d-a066-0fad4e7cd5c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "TeX Live, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/texlive/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 " \[LongDash] on macOS, MacTeX, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/mactex/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/mactex/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/mactex/"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[texlive]"]],
 CellTags->"texlive",ExpressionUUID->"6f3ee899-14c7-4cc3-a237-2eb2a7318e51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"],
 " and TeX Gyre, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre"], None},
